<title>UK: UK refers Cowie buy of British Bus to MMC.</title>
<headline>UK refers Cowie buy of British Bus to MMC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Government said on Thursday that it has referred the acquisition by Cowie Group Plc of British Bus Group Ltd to the Monolopies and Mergers Commission for investigation.  </p>
<p>The government said in a statement that the acquisition raises competition concerns in respect of the bus services market in the U.K., in particular in south London and parts of Surrey and Kent.</p>
<p>Cowie, a British vehicle and leasing bus firm, announced in June that it had made an agreed 282.3 million stg offer for British Bus, the largest privately-owned bus operator in Britain.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
